@startuml seq-storage-routing
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam shadowing false
title Where a write lands — storage profile routing\n(spec: chat-api.service.spec.ts · idb-chat-api.service.spec.ts · routes/shared server specs)
' Aliases match docs/specs/component-map.puml.

actor User
participant "SVC_CHAT\nChatService" as SVC
participant "PORT\nChatApiPort (token CHAT_API)" as PORT
participant "COMPOSITE\nCompositeChatApiService" as COMP
participant "SET_ENV\nEnvironmentService" as ENV
participant "HTTP\nChatApiService" as HTTP
participant "IDB\nIdbChatApiService" as IDB
participant "SERVER\nExpress + sqlite-persistence" as SRV
database "IndexedDB" as IDBX
database "SQLite file" as SQLX

== 1. Which profile is this installation? ==
COMP -> ENV : usesIdb(kind)
ENV --> COMP : storage kind for chats / projects / personas / params / providers
note right of ENV
  profiles: sqlite-all · indexeddb-all · chats-params-idb ·
  content-idb · theme-local.
  The profile comes from GET /api/environment on startup.
end note

== 2. One call, two implementations ==
User -> SVC : create a node
SVC -> PORT : createNode(chatId, data)
PORT -> COMP : same interface, injected by provideChatApi()
alt kind routes to the browser store
  COMP -> IDB : createNode(...)
  IDB -> IDBX : object store write (ordered by position, then creation)
  note right of IDB
    idb-chat-api.service.spec pins the CONTRACT, not the storage:
    lists nodes by position then creation, versioning on
    edit*, branchUser rejects non-user nodes, patchNode validates
    reparent cycles, soft-delete/restore/purge, keepChildren.
  end note
else kind routes to the server
  COMP -> HTTP : createNode(...)
  HTTP -> SRV : POST /chats/:id/nodes
  SRV -> SQLX : INSERT into chat_nodes
  note right of SRV
    routes.test.ts / endpoint-gaps.test.ts / snapshot-persistence.test.ts
    assert the same contract over HTTP — that is why the two
    implementations are kept in lockstep.
  end note
end
IDB --> COMP : ChatNode
HTTP --> COMP : ChatNode
COMP --> PORT : ChatNode
PORT --> SVC : updated tree state (signals)

== 3. Why the specs test both ==
note over COMP
  The specs never mock the port: flows.spec / chat.component.spec
  inject an InMemoryChatApi (test-helpers/) — a THIRD implementation
  of the same interface. That keeps the domain spec independent of
  sqlite vs IndexedDB while still exercising the real ChatService.
end note
note over HTTP
  chat-api.service.spec asserts the HTTP client is stateless:
  URL building, payload shape and error propagation only —
  "no local state — ChatService remains the store / facade".
end note

@enduml
